WEBVTT

00:00:00.119 --> 00:00:09.623
This video shows how to turn on the weighted average on your phone. With it on, each exam type counts toward the final result by its own weight.

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:19.402
Open Settings and go to the School Profile tab. On your phone you can reach Settings from the menu button at the top left.

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:28.835
Scroll down to the Examination Settings card. Weighted Average is currently off, which means report cards use a simple average.

00:00:32.034 --> 00:00:45.594
Tap the switch next to Weighted Average. It turns on, and a message confirms it. Each exam type now counts by its weight, for example Mid-Term 30 percent and Final 70 percent.

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:55.537
Finally, open the Exam Types page and check the weight shown on each card. These weights add up to the final result.

00:01:02.284 --> 00:01:08.476
Weighted average is now on. Report cards will count each exam by its weight.
